BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Corey Harris & Cedric Watson: True Blues
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T230000
DTSTAMP:20261118T115305Z
UID:funcheap-1640883@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Live Music Event
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerThe FreightWhen two of America
 ’s most celebrated roots musicians share a stage\, the result is somethi
 ng rare — a conversation between traditions that have always spoken the 
 same language.\nCorey Harris is a singer\, songwriter\, and bluesman who b
 egan as a New Orleans street musician before traveling the world and perfo
 rming with luminaries including B.B. King\, Taj Mahal\, Buddy Guy\, R.L. B
 urnside\, and Ali Farka Touré. Harris has earned critical acclaim as one 
 of the few contemporary bluesmen able to channel the raw\, direct emotion 
 of acoustic Delta blues while drawing on a remarkable range of influences 
 — from New Orleans to the Caribbean to West Africa — into richly expre
 ssive music that appeals to traditionalists and contemporary listeners ali
 ke. In 2007\, he was awarded a MacArthur Fellowship\, commonly known as th
 e “genius award\,” with the Foundation describing him as an artist who
  “forges an adventurous path marked by deliberate eclecticism.”\n\nCed
 ric Watson is a four-time Grammy-nominated fiddler\, singer\, accordionist
 \, and songwriter who stands as one of the brightest talents to emerge in 
