DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerStanford University\nJoin us a
 s we consider how colonialism continues to shape our world and explore whe
 re\, in the law\, in the archaeological record\, and in art\, we are findi
 ng ways to build more just societies.\n\nInspiring this program is artwork
  by Pedro Lasch\, Coatlicue & Las Meninas: The Stanford Edition\, original
 ly commissioned for a national program and now installed at the Institute.
  In conversation with visual arts professor\, Pedro Lasch\, are internatio
 nal legal scholar\, Tendayi Achiume\, and archaeology professor\, Krish Se
 etah\, moderated by sociologist and IAJS Faculty Director\, Tomás Jiméne
 z.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://justsocieties.stanford.edu/\nDetails: https
