  individuals\, from a Pulitzer Prize–winning data journalist and artist\
 n“Astonishing . . . Chalabi’s taboo-busting transparency about peoples
 ’ financial lives is revolutionary enough. But it’s the pellucid clari
 ty of her data visualizations that will really change how you understand c
 apitalism.”—Alison Bechdel\, bestselling author of Fun Home: A Family 
 Tragicomic\n****\n\nABOUT THIS EVENT\n\nThis event will be hosted by Book 
 Passage at our Corte Madera store.\nFree Admission / Open Seating\nFollowi
 ng the presentation\, there will be a signing line or a meet-and-greet.\nI
 f you are unable to attend the event\, you can still get your copy by clic
 king the “BUY THE BOOK” button above. If you would like a signed or pe
 rsonalized book\, please note that in the order comment field.\nFor any qu
 estions regarding our events\, please contact us at books@bookpassage.com.
 \n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://bookpassage.com/event/mona-chalabi-ten-lives\
 nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/mona-chalabi-ten-lives/\nSource: Funchea
