DESCRIPTION:Let’s Glow SF 2026: SF’s Huge Holiday Projection Arts Fest
 ival (Dec. 4-13)\nDowntown SF\nLet’s Glow SF\, the nation’s largest fr
 ee holiday projection arts festival\, is lighting up downtown San Francisc
 o once again for its sixth and brightest year yet.\nThis all-ages\, family
 -friendly festival runs for 10 dazzling nights from December 4-13\, 2026.\
 nExperience breathtaking animated projections illuminating iconic building
 s across downtown San Francisco\, transforming them into colossal\, colorf
 ul canvases featuring spectacular artwork by 19 artists from around the gl
 obe. It’s a larger-than-life holiday light show that turns the heart of 
 the city into an open-air art gallery after dark.\nLet’s Glow SF\nDecemb
 er 4-13\, 2026 | 6p-10p\nDowntown San Francisco\, 1 Ferry Bldg.\, SF\nFREE
  – RSVP\n\nDowntown SF\n\n2026 Festival Schedule\n\nFriday\, December 4:
  Countdown to Glow opening-night celebration 6–7 PM at Harry Bridges Pla
 za in front of the Ferry Building.\nFriday\, December 4: Festival projecti
 ons 7–10 PM (following Countdown to Glow)\nDecember 5–13: Nightly proj
 ections\, 5:30–10 PM\n\n2026 Show Locations (map)\n\nFerry Building (1 F
 erry Building) – Best viewed from Harry Bridges Plaza.\n101 California S
 t. (101 California St.) – Best viewed from inside 101 California Plaza.\
 nPacific Exchange (301 Pine St.) – Best viewed from 300 Pine Street.\nHo
 bart Building (582 Market St.) – Best viewed from 1 Post Street.\nYerba 
 Buena Lane (Market St.) – Best viewed from Yerba Buena Lane off Market S
 treet.\nSalesforce Tower (4...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://downtownsf.org/
 things-to-do/lets-glow-sf\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/lets-glow-sf-2
 026-sf-huge-holiday-projection-arts-festival-dec-4-13-2/\nSource: Funcheap
  SF
