BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Balboa Christmas Halloween Mystery Marathon ~ First Film
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T183000
DTSTAMP:20261103T193658Z
UID:dothebay-18017447@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Due to forces beyond our control\, we are no longer able to ru
 n the Balboa Halloween Mystery Marathon on Halloween night. In the circums
 tance\, we are hard pivoting to the Balboa Christmas Halloween Mystery Mar
 athon. Same exact run of show\, same exact films selected. Only with more 
 holiday vibes.\n\nThis year\, the Balboa invites you to the BALBOA CHRISTM
 AS HALLOWEEN MOVIE MARATHON.\n\nJoin us any time that evening for the low\
 , low price of $13 as four different programmer select one of their favori
 te horror gems and we run them back to back throughout the night. You won
 ’t know what we’re playing until it’s being announced in the theater
 \, but we can guarantee that all of the films are (a) pre-20th century\, (
 b) never screened in the Bay Area (at least in the past five years)\, and 
 (c) have one curator on our team who think it’s sick as hell. Along with
  that\, we’ll have hot chocolate\, candy canes and special prizes for a 
 mid-way point costume contest for anyone who wants to dress up! Whether yo
 u join for one or stay for all\, come with friends or alone\, we guarantee
  your Saturday at the Balboa will be a night of pure\, sugar high\, blood 
 soaked movie adrenaline.\n\n4:30 PM: Mystery Movie #1 (1979) (4:30 PM - 6 
 PM)\n\n6:10 PM: Mystery Movie #2 (1984) (6:05 PM - 7:30 PM)\n\nCostume Con
 test/Intermission (Fifteen Minutes)\n\n7:40 PM: Mystery Movie #3 (1988) (7
 :45 - 9:11 PM)\n\n9:15 PM: Mystery Movie #4 (1986) (9:15 PM - 10:38 PM)\n\
 n$13\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/20344?siteTok
 en=52wkfzmjpwjjfpz3ye7tz8wscg\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/1
 2/19/balboa-christmas-halloween-mystery-marathon-first-film-tickets\nSourc
 e: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7760419;-122.498063
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35271691/1ad5631f-97de-45a9-84ed-f7df3ec5f209.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261103T193658Z
LOCATION:Balboa Theater\, 3630 Balboa St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/19/balboa-christmas-halloween-myst
 ery-marathon-first-film-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Floating Features: A Christmas Story
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T203000
DTSTAMP:20261020T194441Z
UID:dothebay-17757310@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Based on the humorous writings of author Jean Shepherd\, this 
 beloved holiday movie follows the wintry exploits of youngster Ralphie Par
 ker (Peter Billingsley)\, who spends most of his time dodging a bully (Zac
 k Ward) and dreaming of his ideal Christmas gift\, a “Red Ryder air rifl
 e.” Frequently at odds with his cranky dad (Darren McGavin) but comforte
 d by his doting mother (Melinda Dillon)\, Ralphie struggles to make it to 
 Christmas Day with his glasses and his hopes intact.\n\nAbout Floating Fea
 tures\n\nSan Francisco Legacy Businesses Red and White Fleet and The Roxie
  are partnering to turn the hybrid electric vessel Enhydra into a sailing 
 cinema for a limited run of nighttime film cruises on the Bay. Join us thi
 s autumn for a 2-hour twilight cruise and a feature film handpicked by the
  Roxie. Our electric vessel means no engine noise and a totally unique al 
 fresco movie experience.\n\nFull schedule available here.\n\nRuntime\n\n1h
  33m\n\nYear\n\n1983\n\nDirector\n\nBob Clark\n\nFormat\n\nDCP\n\nFirst Sh
 owing\n\nDecember 19\, 2026\n\nCategories\n\nFloating Features\n\n\,\n\nFe
 atured\, Floating Features\n\nTickets: https://www.redandwhite.com/floatin
 g-features\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/19/floating-featu
 res-a-christmas-story-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34022746/d3ff83de-c8be-456c-a433-ecf48b4aa6e3.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261020T194441Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/19/floating-features-a-christmas-s
 tory-tickets
END:VEVENT
