BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Japanese Tea Garden’s Free Admission Hour (Golden Gate Park)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261221T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261221T100000
DTSTAMP:20261027T152452Z
UID:funcheap-1644522@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Outdoors
DESCRIPTION:Japanese Tea Garden’s Free Admission Hour (Golden Gate Park)
 \nJapanese Tea Garden\nThe Japanese Tea Garden provides visitors from arou
 nd the world with an opportunity to experience the natural beauty\, tranqu
 ility\, and harmony of a Japanese-style garden in the heart of San Francis
 co’s Golden Gate Park.\nOriginally created as a “Japanese Village” e
 xhibit for the 1894 California Midwinter International Exposition\, the Ja
 panese Tea Garden endures as one of the most popular attractions in San Fr
 ancisco\, featuring classic elements such as an arched drum bridge\, pagod
 as\, stone lanterns\, stepping stone paths\, native Japanese plants\, sere
 ne koi ponds\, and a zen garden. Cherry blossom trees bloom throughout the
  garden in March and April.\nAdmission to the Japanese Tea Garden is free 
 for San Francisco residents with valid ID. Free hours for everyone (even n
 on-residents) are 9-10 am every Monday\, Wednesday and Friday.\n\nPlease n
 ote that hours and costs change frequently.\nJapanese Tea Garden\n75 Hagiw
 ara Tea Garden\, Golden Gate Park\, SF\nFREE for San Francisco Residents w
 / ID\nFREE for Everyone from 9-10 am on Mondays\, Wednesdays and Fridays\n
 Non Resident Fees\nAdults: $12-16 (depends on season)\n(February – Novem
 ber) $14\n(December – January) $12\n(Weekends year-round) $16\nSeniors (
 ages 65+ w/ID) $7\nYouth (ages 12-17) $7\nChildren (ages 5-11) $3\nChildre
 n (under 5) FREE\nHours Of Operation\nLast entry 30 minutes before closing
 \nSpring – Summer Hours\nMarch – October\n9am – 5:45pm\nFall – Win
 ter Hours\nNovembe...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.japaneseteagardensf.
 com/vist\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/japanese-tea-gardens-free-admis
 sion-hour-golden-gate-park-464/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/japane
 seteagarden-scaled-e1595352236641.jpeg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261027T152452Z
LOCATION:Japanese Tea Garden\, 75 Hagiwara Tea Garden Dr\, San Francisco\,
  CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/japanese-tea-gardens-free-admission-hour-golde
 n-gate-park-464/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Programa de gestión de contingencias en español
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261221T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261221T113000
DTSTAMP:20261023T171442Z
UID:dothebay-17821080@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:LGBTQ
DESCRIPTION:¿Le interesa cambiar\, reducir\, reevaluar o dejar de consumi
 r estimulantes como la metanfetamina o la cocaína?\n\nOfrecemos un progra
 ma de gestión de contingencias en español en nuestra agencia asociada\, 
 el Proyecto Gubbio.\n\nEste programa es un programa de refuerzo positivo d
 e 12 semanas/24 sesiones con servicios médicos\, asesoramiento individual
 \, gestión de casos y grupo de apoyo\, y todos los servicios se brindan e
 n español.\n\nPara obtener más información o unirse al grupo\, comuníq
 uese con Maricruz al 415-632-9722 o envíe un correo electrónico a mmoren
 o@sfaf.org.\n\n___________\n\nContingency management program in Spanish\n\
 nInterested in changing\, reducing\, re-evaluating\, or stopping your use 
 of stimulants such as meth or cocaine?\n\nWe offer a contingency managemen
 t program in Spanish at our partner agency\, the Gubbio Project.\n\nThis p
 rogram is a positive reinforcement 12 week/24-session program with medical
  services\, individual counseling\, case management\, and support group wi
 th all services provided in Spanish.\n\nFor more information or to join th
 e group\, please contact Maricruz at 415-632-9722 or mmoreno@sfaf.org.\n\n
 Tickets: https://resources.sfaf.org/event/programa-de-gestion-de-contingen
 cias-en-espanol/2026-12-21/\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/
 21/programa-de-gestion-de-contingencias-en-espanol-tickets\nSource: DoTheB
 ay
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023T171442Z
LOCATION:San Francisco AIDS Foundation\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94102
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/21/programa-de-gestion-de-continge
 ncias-en-espanol-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Carol
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261221T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261221T200000
DTSTAMP:20261102T193355Z
UID:dothebay-18016745@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Presented by OUTlook and Frameline\n\nDubbed “SF’s hottest
  new holiday tradition” by the San Francisco Chronicle\, Frameline’s f
 ourth annual Carol Day returns to its home at the Roxie Theater. Shake up 
 your martinis\, don your gloves (and gay apparel) for a costume contest\, 
 and get ready to be flung out of space — again.\n\nSet during Christmast
 ime in 1950s New York\, Todd Haynes’ adaptation of Patricia Highsmith’
 s The Price of Salt centers on shy\, aspiring photographer Therese Belivet
  (Rooney Mara)\, whose world changes when she meets the elegant Carol Aird
  (Cate Blanchett). As Carol struggles to maintain custody of her daughter 
 amid a heated divorce\, she and Therese develop a secret-yet-passionate ro
 mance that changes them both irrevocably.\n\nFeaturing a stunning screenpl
 ay from Phyllis Nagy\; memorable supporting turns from Sarah Paulson\, Kyl
 e Chandler\, and Jake Lacy\; and wholly transportive production design and
  costuming\, Carol remains one of queer cinema’s most exquisite films.\n
 \nRuntime\n\n1h 58m\n\nYear\n\n2015\n\nDirector\n\nTodd Haynes\n\nFormat\n
 \nDCP\n\nFirst Showing\n\nDecember 21\, 2026\n\nCategories\n\nOUTlook\n\n\
 ,\n\nFeatured\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/2245
 2?siteToken=4m48btf3yavn7xjk5yxk6nc40c\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/even
 ts/2026/12/21/carol-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35226407/bd640154-a746-457c-b427-3051960aaf3c.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261102T193355Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/21/carol-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SF Arcade Bar “Emporium” 8 Free Game Tokens for “Industry Ni
 ght” (Every Monday)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261221T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261222T020000
DTSTAMP:20261027T152452Z
UID:funcheap-1644505@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Fun Games
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerSF Arcade Bar “Emporium” 8
  Free Game Tokens for “Industry Night” (Every Monday)\nEmporium SF\nEm
 porium Arcade Bar San Francisco\, the dynamic venue known for its classic 
 arcade games\, colorful\, fun-loving atmosphere\, and renowned drink menu\
 , now offers 8 free game tokens for anyone in “the industry” – so we
 ’re assuming barstaff\, restaurant staff\, nightlife staff.\nMonday Nigh
 ts are for the Industry! Every Monday night come join us for some drink sp
 ecials and if you are part of our industry you get 8 tokens!\nFeaturing Co
 nsole Encounters! Get to play some retro games on our 50′ HD screen!\n\n
 Emporium Arcade Bar offers guests a variety of games\, including classic a
 rcade favorites\, pool tables\, pinball\, foosball\, and many more. Their 
 curated bar purveys local craft beer selections\, an innovative cocktail p
 rogram\, boozy slushies\, and an expansive liquor list.\nEmporium Arcade B
 ar’s Industry Night\n616 Divisadero St.\, San Francisco\nEvery Monday | 
 6 pm to 2 am\nFREE with 8 free game tokens for “industry” people\n\nEm
 porium Arcade Bar San Francisco is open daily for guests 21 years or older
 .\nWe’re told “most” games only require one token\, so that’s four
  games you can play for free every Monday night.\n\nEmporium Arcade Bar is
