CATEGORIES:Art Museums
DESCRIPTION:“Legion of Honor” Museum Free Day (First Tuesdays)\n© Ste
 phanHoerold Getty Images Signature via Canva.com\nThe Legion of Honor disp
 lays a collection of 4\,000 years of ancient and European art in an exquis
 ite Beaux-Arts building in an unforgettable setting overlooking the Golden
  Gate Bridge.\nNormally\, general admission is $20 for adults\, but on the
  first Tuesday of the month\, admission is free.\n\nThis offer applies onl
 y to the permanent collection galleries. Full-price admission to special e
 xhibitions still applies.\nWe suggest booking your tickets in advance onli
 ne.\nFree admission may also be redeemed by visiting the ticketing and mem
 bership desks\, pending availability.\n\nOther Free & Discounted Admission
  Deals\nThe Legion of Honor offers several programs for free or reduced ad
 mission to permanent galleries and special exhibitions. Details on these p
 rograms are outlined below.\nWe will require timed tickets for every visit
 or\, including general admission. To ensure your preferred time slot\, ple
 ase reserve your entry date and time in advance online.\n\nFree Saturdays 
 for Bay Area Residents\nReserve Online and Skip the Line\nEvery Saturday\,
  the Legion of Honor offers free general admission to all residents of the
  nine Bay Area counties. Saturdays feature engaging art experiences for th
 e entire family\, including art making\, gallery guides\, and tours with d
 iscussion and sketching in the permanent galleries.\n\nThis offer applies 
 only to the permanent collection galleries. Full-price admission...\n\nFre
 e\n\nTickets: https://legionofhonor.famsf.org/free-reduced-admission\nDeta
 ils: https://sf.funcheap.com/legion-of-honor-museum-free-day-first-tuesday
 s-69/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/legion
 honor.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008T104232Z
LOCATION:Legion of Honor\, 100 34th Avenue\, San Francisco\, CA 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/legion-of-honor-museum-free-day-first-tuesdays
 -69/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SF’s Conservatory of Flowers Free First Tuesdays (Golden Gate Pa
 rk)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270105T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270105T163000
DTSTAMP:20261107T005802Z
UID:funcheap-1646289@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art Museums
DESCRIPTION:SF’s Conservatory of Flowers Free First Tuesdays (Golden Gat
 e Park)\nConservatory of Flowers\nWhether you’re a native San Franciscan
 \, a visitor from the other side of the world\, or a budding botanist\, th
 e Conservatory of Flowers\, located in Golden Gate Park\, offers an intima
 te\, up-close experience with nearly 2\,000 species of rare\, exotic\, and
  endangered plants from more than 50 different countries.\nOpened in 1879\
 , the wood and glass greenhouse is the oldest existing conservatory of its
  kind in the Western Hemisphere.\nConservatory of Flowers’ Free Admissio
 n Day\nFirst Tuesday of Every Month\n100 JFK Dr.\, Golden Gate Park\, San 
 Francisco\nFREE for everyone\nAdmission is normally free for SF residents 
 ($12 for non-SF residents)\, but it’s free for all visitors on the first
  Tuesday of every month.\nThe Conservatory will also continue offering fre
 e or reduced admission through Museums for All\, a program to bring free o
 r reduced admission to San Francisco residents who receive public beneﬁt
 s\, including Medi-Cal and CalFresh. Plus\, there’s free admission for M
 ilitary & Veterans and children 4 and under.\n\nHours:\nThursday-Tuesday\n
 10am – 4:30pm\nLast entry at 4pm\nFree Day: First Tuesday of the Month\n
 Enjoy our winter light show\, Photosynthesis\, beginning 30 minutes after 
 sunset every night. The show is free to the public and is about 30 minutes
  long.\nClosed: Wednesdays for weekly maintenance\; 2026 Annual Maintenanc
 e Closure: January 21\, 2026-February 4\, 2026.\n\nUpcoming SF’s Conserv
 atory of Flowe...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://conservatoryofflowers.org/vi
 sit/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-conservatory-of-flowers-free-fi
 rst-tuesdays-golden-gate-park-74/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/07/Conser
 vatory-Of-Flowers-San-Francisco-1280x6401.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261107T005802Z
LOCATION:Conservatory of Flowers\, 100 John F Kennedy Dr\, San Francisco\,
  CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-conservatory-of-flowers-free-first-tuesday
 s-golden-gate-park-74/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SF’s Cartoon Art Museum’s “Pay What You Wish” Day (First T
 uesdays)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270105T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270105T170000
DTSTAMP:20261008T104232Z
UID:funcheap-1641676@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art Museums
DESCRIPTION:SF’s Cartoon Art Museum’s “Pay What You Wish” Day (Fir
 st Tuesdays)\nCartoon Art Museum\nFounded in 1984\, the Cartoon Art Museum
  has something for everyone—from comic strips\, comic books and anime to
  political cartoons\, graphic novels and underground comix. People of all 
 ages can view original cartoon art at exhibitions and screenings\, produce
  their own comics and animation at classes and workshops\, research deeply
  into our collection and library\, and mix and mingle with professional an
 d aspiring cartoonists. This unique institution houses approximately 7\,00
 0 original pieces in our permanent collection and attracts more than 30\,0
 00 visitors annually.\nFirst Tuesday “Pay What You Wish” Day\nFirst Tu
 esdays | 11 am to 5 pm\nCartoon Art Museum\, 781 Beach Street\, San Franci
 sco\nFREE Admission\nPay What You Wish Days create affordable experiences 
 for all to ignite imaginations and foster the next generation of visual st
 orytellers by celebrating the history of cartoon art\, its role in society
 \, and its universal appeal with a visit to the Cartoon Art Museum. Set yo
 ur own admission price and find inspiration through viewing original art\,
  exploring the reading room or enjoying family-oriented activities in thei
 r kids corner.\nCartoon Art Museum Admission\n\nAdults – $10\nSan Franci
 sco Resident – $7\nStudents/Senior/Military/Educator (with valid ID) –
  $6\nKids (6-12) – $4\nChildren (5 and Younger) – FREE\nCartoon Art Mu
 seum Members – FREE\nThe first Tuesday of every month is our Pay What Yo
 u Wish Day....\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.cartoonart.org/visit\nDetai
 ls: https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-cartoon-art-museums-pay-what-you-wish-day-
 first-tuesdays-34/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/12/154398
 19_10154650476372787_559204237688024280_n-1.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008T104232Z
LOCATION:Cartoon Art Museum\, 781 Beach Street\, San Francisco\, Californi
 a 94109
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-cartoon-art-museums-pay-what-you-wish-day-
 first-tuesdays-34/
END:VEVENT
