SUMMARY:MoAD: Museum of the African Diaspora Free Museum Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270109T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270109T170000
DTSTAMP:20261012T211826Z
UID:funcheap-1642137@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art Museums
DESCRIPTION:MoAD: Museum of the African Diaspora Free Museum Day (SF)\nMOA
 D\nMoAD\, a contemporary art museum\, celebrates Black cultures\, ignites 
 challenging conversations\, and inspires learning through the global lens 
 of the African Diaspora.\nMonthly Free Day\nMoAD hosts a ‘‍THRIVE @ Mo
 AD Community Day’ every second Saturday with free admission to all of it
 s exhibitions. Check the events calendar to confirm\, as free days sometim
 es change.\nMoAD Hours\nMonday – CLOSED\nTuesday – Sunday\, 11 am – 
 5 pm\nThursday – Noon to 8 pm\n‍\nAdmission\n– General Admission –
  $15\n– Seniors\, Students\, Educators – $7\n– Youth (Under 12) – 
 Free\n– Members & Active Duty Military – Free\n\nVisiting with kids:\n
 Kids and families receive a warm welcome at MoAD. Our elevator makes it ea
 sy to navigate with a stroller\, and kids ages 12 and under always receive
  free admission.\nMuseums For All:\nVisit MoAD through Museums for All\n
 – Through Museums for All\, those receiving food assistance (SNAP benefi
 ts) can gain free or reduced admission to more than 700 museums throughout
  the United States simply by presenting their EBT card. Free entry is avai
 lable for up to 4 individuals per EBT card.\n\nSpecial Exhibitions for 202
 6\nContinuum: MoAD Over TimeMoAD ArtistsOctober 1\, 2025 – March 1\, 202
 6Museum of the African Diaspora (MoAD)A special exhibition highlighting th
 e evolution of MoAD artists over time.\n\nUNBOUND: Art\, Blackness & the U
 niverseCurated by Key Jo LeeOctober 1\, 2025 – August 16\, 2026Museum of
  the African Diaspora (MoAD)Spanning a...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.
 moadsf.org/visit\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/moad-museum-of-the-afri
 can-diaspora-free-museum-day-sf-47/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/62ea74
 7d1e6f2da1381bac86_MoAD-Building_Exterior_Compressed.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261012T211826Z
LOCATION:Museum of the African Diaspora\, 685 Mission St\, San Francisco\,
  CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/moad-museum-of-the-african-diaspora-free-museu
 m-day-sf-47/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Beginner Parkour “Urban Ninja” Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270109T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270109T133000
DTSTAMP:20261115T162545Z
UID:funcheap-1647386@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Sports Fitness
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerFree Beginner Parkour “Urban
  Ninja” Class\nSF Parkour\nSF Parkour hosts a free Beginner’s Parkour 
 Class at noon on the second Saturday of each month. It is geared towards f
 irst timers and lasts 1.5 hours.\nLocation: Each month the location rotate
 s through Sunnyvale\, UC Berkeley and the Embarcadero in SF. Please check 
 the SF Parkour Facebook page to make sure you have the right date and loca
 tion before heading out.\n\nThe emphasis will be on controlled progression
  and will cover: philosophy of parkour\, training\, conditioning and safet
 y tips\, and basic movements such as vaults\, landings and rolls. Taking p
 hotos/videos at this session is discouraged. Attendees are also welcome to
  hang out\, continue training\, or have an open jam after the class ends.\
 nAdditional Info:\n\nThe scheduled dates and times will be adhered to unle
 ss otherwise specified due to holidays\, conflicting events\, special even
 ts\, visiting guests\, etc. This way attendees can plan well ahead of time
 .\nAll ages\, sexes\, and experience levels are welcome. Ages 18 and under
  must have parental permission.\nBeginners are always welcome and can get 
 help at any of the sessions.\nEach of the sessions will include warm ups\,
  help for beginners\, conditioning and training\, open jamming\, cool down
 s\, and clean-up time.\nWear comfortable clothing you can move freely in\,
  a good pair of running shoes\, and bring along some water.\n\n– Updated
  6/4/19 – Event info last checked via website\n\nUpcoming Free Beginner 
 Park...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.facebook.com/pg/SFParkour/events/?
 ref=page_internal\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/free-beginner-parkour-
 urban-ninja-class-132/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/03/Screen
 -Shot-2018-09-07-at-11.50.06-PM.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261115T162545Z
LOCATION:Secret Location
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/free-beginner-parkour-urban-ninja-class-132/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eco SF School Farm Volunteer Work Day | SF
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270109T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270109T160000
DTSTAMP:20261116T064237Z
UID:funcheap-1647436@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lectures Workshops
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerEco SF School Farm Volunteer W
 ork Day | SF\nNational Park Service\nCome join a volunteer work party at T
 he School Farm every second Saturday from noon to 4 pm to lend a hand and 
 learn about farm work.\nAll skill levels and abilities are welcome\, even 
 for moral support and comic relief. They will provide some water and maybe
  a snack\, and plenty of well worn gloves\, but If you’d like\, bring so
 me more refreshments to share or your favorite personal protective equipme
 nt. For more info\, contact sam@eco-sf.org.\n\nThe School Farm is located 
 on the campus of the Academy of Arts and Sciences and the School of the Ar
 ts – 555 Portola Dr. San Francisco. Enter gate on O’shaughnessy Blvd j
 ust before it crosses Portola. It’s close to 36\, 44\, 48\, and 52 Muni 
 lines. From the parking area at the top\, proceed on foot to the right\, d
 own the hill towards the athletic field. Limited parking is available furt
 her down the driveway at the loading dock\, but please do not park on the 
